A||N||2||wxxo||Need an exorcist for my wipers||||1||
Z||000000||wxxo||10-13-2000||04:03 PM||||im thinking that i need an exorcist for my windshield wipers. when i use my turn signal they come on and wont stop for a while. guess its a short somewhere but is there an easy fix for this. would a new stalk fix the problem or do i need to tear into the column?? thanks in advance for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Bob Englert||10-13-2000||05:51 PM||||From my personal experience if the wipers go on randomly when you operate the turn signal you will probably need to replace the wiper switch in the steering column.  It isn't really difficult but it is time consuming to get everything off needed to reach the switch. You will need to remove the steering wheel, lock plate, column cover, tilt lever, and ingition key tumbler to get to the wiper switch.  I did not get the key buzzer contact back in properly on my daughters car, otherwise, it is more inconvienent than difficult.<P>The stalk is just a stcik as far as the turn signal and wipers are concerned.  Both of these switches are inside the column with the stalk acting as a lever to manipulate both.  <P>Advance Auto sells a wiper switch GP Sorensen #DS170 for about $55.  It is also available from PartsAmerica.com Search for the part #.<P>Generally the stalk would only need to be repalced if it has phyically broken or the cruise switch or wiring is broken.  <P>Good luck...<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-13-2000||07:10 PM||||probly get it at carparts.com wrenchead.com or napaonline.com but check your local shops first. most times when you figure shipping the parts you get online aren't a savings.||||reg||1
